cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AlphaBench, please cite it as below."
title: "AlphaBench: walk-forward equity return forecasting and backtesting"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible platform for testing whether supervised models can predict the sign of
  short-horizon equity returns well enough to beat buy-and-hold after costs. Reports a
  null result: across a full baseline ladder (persistence through a stacked ensemble),
  two independent markets, and a sealed single-use holdout, walk-forward ROC-AUC sits at
  0.49-0.52 and no edge survives realistic transaction costs. The contribution is the
  validation harness -- expanding-window walk-forward with purge and embargo, structural
  leakage defences enforced by tests that fail the build, block-bootstrap confidence
  intervals, and a deflated Sharpe ratio correcting for search effort -- which is what
  makes the negative result trustworthy rather than merely unsurprising.
type: software
